{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 537529, "name": "Jason C", "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T02:57:04.735Z", "cooked": "<p>As noted in: <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/rustup-package-does-not-provide-rustup/161507/4\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Rustup package does not provide rustup - #4 by decathorpe</a></p>\n<p>Installing the <code>rustup</code> package does not actually provide the <code>rustup</code> binary. It provides <code>rustup-init</code> which can be run to do the initial installation of <code>rustup</code>.</p>\n<p>I was recently bit by this, because even though I’ve had <code>rustup</code> installed for quite some time, I failed to realize it was extremely outdated (over 2 years outdated!). Updating the <code>rustup</code> package doesn’t update the <code>rustup</code> binary, just as it doesn’t install it.</p>\n<p>Normally, <code>rustup</code> is capable of self-updating. But using the <code>rustup</code> installed by <code>rustup-init</code> provided by the <code>rustup</code> package to run <code>rustup self update</code> just leads to:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">error: self-update is disabled for this build of rustup\nerror: you should probably use your system package manager to update rustup\n</code></pre>\n<p>It seems like a workaround is to run <code>rustup-init</code> again, but this feels janky and wrong, and also messes with my <code>.bashrc</code> when it doesn’t need to. Given that having the <code>rustup</code> package only provide <code>rustup-init</code> instead of <code>rustup</code> was an intentional decision, what is the intended way for us to actually update <code>rustup</code>? It seems strange that updating the package doesn’t do it, yet the package still disables self-updates.</p>\n<p>If anyone knows where I could find more about the reasoning for the decision to have the <code>rustup</code> package provide <code>rustup-init</code>, I’d be interested in reading up on that, too.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T02:57:04.735Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 31, "reads": 39, "readers_count": 38, "score": 162.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Jason C", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/rustup-package-does-not-provide-rustup/161507/4", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Rustup package does not provide rustup", "clicks": 2}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27408, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 537560, "name": "synx", "username": "ssynxx", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ssynxx/{size}/57658_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T06:09:47.295Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi Jason,</p>\n<p>From what I understand, the Fedora package only provides <code>rustup-init</code>, which has self-updates disabled. Running it installs another copy in <code>~/.cargo/bin/</code>, and that copy isn’t managed by DNF.</p>\n<p>So updating the package doesn’t update the rustup you actually use. The workaround is to run:</p>\n<pre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"><code class=\"lang-bash\">sudo dnf upgrade rustup\nrustup-init -y --no-modify-path --default-toolchain none\n</code></pre>\n<p>You can compare the versions too:</p>\n<pre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"><code class=\"lang-bash\">rustup-init --version\nrustup --version\n</code></pre>\n<p>Another option is to use the installer from <a href=\"https://rustup.rs\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://rustup.rs</a>, but then DNF won’t manage rustup anymore.</p>\n<p>Not sure about the exact reason behind Fedora’s packaging choice. The <a href=\"https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/rustup\">Fedora package spec and changelog</a> might be worth checking.</p>\n<p>I think the package description could explain this better, since updating the RPM doesn’t update the rustup binary in your home directory. Maybe a Bugzilla request would be worth it.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T06:09:47.295Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 7, "reads": 38, "readers_count": 37, "score": 62.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "synx", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/rustup", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 3}, {"url": "https://rustup.rs", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "rustup.rs - The Rust toolchain installer", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 33265, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 537653, "name": "Fabio Valentini", "username": "decathorpe", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T13:05:59.392Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello, rustup package maintainer here.</p>\n<p>The primary motivation for providing rustup as a package in Fedora is so that you don’t have to <code>curl | bash</code> (which is generally considered … erm … “questionable” from a security perspective).</p>\n<p>The way rustup and its self-update functionality work are kind of incompatible with providing a fully functional “rustup” setup just by installing it:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>We can’t provide the usual symlinks that rustup would set up for your toolchain (i.e. rustc, cargo, clippy, rustfmt, etc.) in the system-wide $PATH because those would conflict with the system packages for those same tools.</li>\n<li>The self-update functionality would (I think?) overwrite the system-provided rustup multicall binaries with ones downloaded from rustup.rs - but <em>not</em> doing that is the entire reason why people would install rustup from the package repos.</li>\n</ol>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ssynxx\" data-display-name=\"synx\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ssynxx/48/57658_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> synx:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>rustup-init -y --no-modify-path --default-toolchain none</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So I think running ↑ after a rustup package update really is the only easy way to keep your rustup install up-to-date.</p>\n<p>Since packages aren’t allowed to modify users’ $HOME directories, I think this might also be the only way this <em>can</em> work. But if anybody has an idea for how to improve this from a packaging perspective, I’m open to suggestions.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T13:05:59.392Z", "reply_count": 2, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 31, "readers_count": 30, "score": 96.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Fabio Valentini", "primary_group_name": "fesco", "flair_name": "fesco", "flair_url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/f/af3a1ba1ca92e6d3195851ee9e6829a8a2e00586.png", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 64, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Fedora Engineering Steering Committee", "title_is_group": true, "reply_to_user": {"id": 33265, "username": "ssynxx", "name": "synx", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ssynxx/{size}/57658_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 5}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1009, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/3", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 5}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 5, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 537725, "name": "Jason C", "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T16:52:02.203Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for your response. There’s something I don’t really understand though, forgive my ignorance.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-fesco\" data-username=\"decathorpe\" data-display-name=\"Fabio Valentini\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/48/29651_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Fabio Valentini:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>The self-update functionality would (I think?) overwrite the system-provided rustup multicall binaries with ones downloaded from rustup.rs - but <em>not</em> doing that is the entire reason why people would install rustup from the package repos.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What do you mean by “system-provided rustup multicall binaries”? Are you referring to <code>rustup</code>? If so, I think you might be wrong? Updating using <code>rustup-init</code> would do the same thing, wouldn’t it? At least, that seems to be what is implied here:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/environment-variables.html\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/favicon-de23e50b.svg\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"184\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/environment-variables.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">rust-lang.github.io</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    \n\n<h3><a href=\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/environment-variables.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Environment variables - The rustup book</a></h3>\n\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<blockquote>\n<p>RUSTUP_VERSION (default: none). Overrides the rustup version (e.g. 1.27.1) to be downloaded when executing rustup-init.sh or rustup self update.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>So in order to not do that, you’d need to commit to never updating <code>rustup</code>. Which you can achieve by just doing <code>rustup set auto-self-update disable</code>. Which would still allow those who want to receive updates to <code>rustup</code> to take advantage of the self-update functionality.</p>\n<p>The reason I install <code>rustup</code> from the package repos is because I use an atomic version of Fedora, so I generally prefer using Fedora packages since they should usually account for any weirdness that comes with that. I feel more confident that Fedora packages will just work on my system by the time they make it to stable.</p>\n<p>Thanks again for your response and for your work packaging this. If I’m misunderstanding something, I’m happy to be corrected.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T16:52:02.203Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 9.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Jason C", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/environment-variables.html", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Environment variables - The rustup book", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 1009, "username": "decathorpe", "name": "Fabio Valentini", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27408, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 537733, "name": "Fabio Valentini", "username": "decathorpe", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T17:11:53.722Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cosmic-atomic-fan\" data-display-name=\"Jason C\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jason C:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What do you mean by “system-provided rustup multicall binaries”?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Running rustup-init creates symlinks in (modified) $PATH as rustc, cargo, etc. that point <em>at itself</em>. If you look at the contents of <code>~/.cargo/bin/</code> you can see that `cargo, rustc, rustfmt, etc. are all symbolic links that point at rustup. The executable behaves differently (e.g. it behaves as if it were cargo if it is <em>called</em> as “cargo”, but it behaves as if it were rustc if it is <em>called</em> as rustc, etc. - that’s what “multicall” refers to).</p>\n<p>So I assume that the self-update functionality (that is disabled in Fedora package builds) would overwrite rustup with rustup downloaded from <a href=\"http://rust-lang.org\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">rust-lang.org</a>, making the executable from the Fedora package unused, and have all those symlinks just point at the freshly downloaded rustup executable.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cosmic-atomic-fan\" data-display-name=\"Jason C\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jason C:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>RUSTUP_VERSION (default: none). Overrides the rustup version (e.g. 1.27.1) to be downloaded when executing rustup-init.sh or rustup self update.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This seems to only apply to the shell script wrapper around rustup-init, (i.e. rustup-init.sh), not rustup-init itself. This wrapper is only used as an architecture-independent way to download the <em>actual</em> rustup-init for the current architecture, and it’s not even shipped in the Fedora package for rustup, so I don’t think it’s relevant here.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T17:11:53.722Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 24.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Fabio Valentini", "primary_group_name": "fesco", "flair_name": "fesco", "flair_url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/f/af3a1ba1ca92e6d3195851ee9e6829a8a2e00586.png", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 64, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "http://rust-lang.org", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Rust Programming Language", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "Fedora Engineering Steering Committee", "title_is_group": true, "reply_to_user": {"id": 27408, "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "name": "Jason C", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1009, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "totally", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 537739, "name": "Jason C", "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T17:36:11.515Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-fesco\" data-username=\"decathorpe\" data-display-name=\"Fabio Valentini\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/48/29651_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Fabio Valentini:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This seems to only apply to the shell script wrapper around rustup-init, (i.e. rustup-init.sh), not rustup-init itself. This wrapper is only used as an architecture-independent way to download the <em>actual</em> rustup-init for the current architecture, and it’s not even shipped in the Fedora package for rustup, so I don’t think it’s relevant here.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah, I think that was my misunderstanding. I didn’t realize <code>rustup-init</code> and <code>rustup-init.sh</code> were different. Thanks!</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-10-13T17:36:11.515Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 19.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Jason C", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 1009, "username": "decathorpe", "name": "Fabio Valentini", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27408, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 541884, "name": "Jason C", "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-11-01T21:33:36.786Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-fesco\" data-username=\"decathorpe\" data-display-name=\"Fabio Valentini\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/48/29651_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Fabio Valentini:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The way rustup and its self-update functionality work are kind of incompatible with providing a fully functional “rustup” setup just by installing it</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Just so you know, it seems this discussion has spawned an issue for improving support for packaging: <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rustup/issues/5149\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Better setup experience for third-party packagers? · Issue #5149 · rust-lang/rustup · GitHub</a></p>\n<p>It looks like it might be a good idea to reach out to the maintainer if you get a chance:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I wonder whether this is a good opportunity to get in touch with the packagers to see how they think the flow should be on their side… however I might have difficulties in getting the contacts I need <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/eyes.png?v=15\" title=\":eyes:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":eyes:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>They might be able to have <code>rustup-init</code> do a symlink instead of a copy, which I think would make it so updating the <code>rustup</code> package would update <code>rustup</code> without needing to re-run <code>rustup-init</code>.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-11-01T21:33:36.786Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 13, "readers_count": 12, "score": 17.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204625, "topic_slug": "what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date", "display_username": "Jason C", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rustup/issues/5149", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Better setup experience for third-party packagers? · Issue #5149 · rust-lang/rustup · GitHub", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 1009, "username": "decathorpe", "name": "Fabio Valentini", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 27408, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "eyes", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}], "stream": [537529, 537560, 537653, 537725, 537733, 537739, 541884]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 22], [7, 2]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 865, "name": "updates", "slug": "updates"}, {"id": 723, "name": "packages", "slug": "packages"}, {"id": 394, "name": "rpm", "slug": "rpm"}, {