ll, "description": "Original Poster", "user": {"id": 4387, "username": "boredsquirrel", "name": "boredsquirrel", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/boredsquirrel/{size}/38156_2.png", "trust_level": 4}}, {"extras": null, "description": "Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 22345, "username": "thephatlee", "name": "Marko Jokinen", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/thephatlee/{size}/39811_2.png", "trust_level": 3}}, {"extras": "latest", "description": "Most Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 25330, "username": "clseibold", "name": "CLSeibold", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/b193c8/{size}.png", "trust_level": 1}}]}, {"fancy_title": "Package Rust applications, is it really worth it?", "id": 39779, "title": "Package Rust applications, is it really worth it?", "slug": "package-rust-applications-is-it-really-worth-it", "posts_count": 4, "reply_count": 1, "highest_post_number": 4, "image_url": null, "created_at": "2022-06-10T17:41:51.933Z", "last_posted_at": "2022-06-19T01:30:42.425Z", "bumped": true, "bumped_at": "2022-06-19T01:30:42.425Z", "archetype": "regular", "unseen": false, "pinned": false, "unpinned": null, "visible": true, "closed": false, "archived": false, "bookmarked": null, "liked": null, "tags": [{"id": 304, "name": "package-maintainers", "slug": "package-maintainers"}, {"id": 303, "name": "rust-sig", "slug": "rust-sig"}], "tags_descriptions": {"package-maintainers": "Packaging RPMs for everyone!", "rust-sig": "Rust Programming Language SIG"}, "like_count": 6, "views": 647, "category_id": 7, "featured_link": null, "op_like_count": 2, "has_accepted_answer": false, "posters": [{"extras": "latest", "description": "Original Poster, Most Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 231, "username": "gbcox", "name": "Gerald B  Cox", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gbcox/{size}/6676_2.png", "moderator": true, "trust_level": 2}}, {"extras": null, "description": "Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 2089, "username": "oturpe", "name": "Otto Liljalaakso", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/oturpe/{size}/4693_2.png", "trust_level": 2}}, {"extras": null, "description": "Recent Poster", "user": {"id": 319, "username": "blaise", "name": "Blaise R Pabon", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/blaise/{size}/28719_2.png", "trust_level": 2}}]}], "summarizable": false, "has_cached_summary": false, "has_livestream": null, "valid_reactions": ["heart", "classic_smiley", "bluethumb", "party", "eureka", "totally", "fedora", "eyes"], "accepted_answers": [{"id": 537653, "name": "Fabio Valentini", "username": "decathorpe", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-13T13:05:59.392Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello, rustup package maintainer here.</p>\n<p>The primary motivation for providing rustup as a package in Fedora is so that you don’t have to <code>curl | bash</code> (which is generally considered … erm … “questionable” from a security perspective).</p>\n<p>The way rustup and its self-update functionality work are kind of incompatible with providing a fully functional “rustup” setup just by installing it:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>We can’t provide the usual symlinks that rustup would set up for your toolchain (i.e. rustc, cargo, clippy, rustfmt, etc.) in the system-wide $PATH because those would conflict with the system packages for those same tools.</li>\n<li>The self-update functionality would (I think?) overwrite the system-provided rustup multicall binaries with ones downloaded from rustup.rs - but <em>not</em> doing that is the entire reason why people would install rustup from the package repos.</li>\n</ol>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ssynxx\" data-display-name=\"synx\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"204625\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ssynxx/48/57658_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> synx:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>rustup-init -y --no-modify-path --default-toolchain none</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So I think running ↑ after a rustup package update really is the only easy way to keep your rustup install up-to-date.</p>\n<p>Since packages aren’t allowed to modify users’ $HOME directories, I think this might also be the only way this <em>can</em> work. But if anybody has an idea for how to improve this from a packaging perspective, I’m open to suggestions.</p>", "post_number": 3, "topic_id": 204625, "url": "/t/what-is-the-correct-way-to-keep-rustup-up-to-date/204625/3"}], "has_accepted_answer": true, "shared_issue_count": 0, "can_create_shared_issue": false, "shared_issue_visible": true, "discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id": null, "discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url": "https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/", "details": {"can_edit": false, "notification_level": 1, "participants": [{"id": 27408, "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "name": "Jason C", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "post_count": 4, "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "trust_level": 1}, {"id": 1009, "username": "decathorpe", "name": "Fabio Valentini", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/decathorpe/{size}/29651_2.png", "post_count": 2, "primary_group_name": "fesco", "flair_name": "fesco", "flair_url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/f/af3a1ba1ca92e6d3195851ee9e6829a8a2e00586.png", "flair_color": "", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_group_id": 64, "trust_level": 2}, {"id": 33265, "username": "ssynxx", "name": "synx", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ssynxx/{size}/57658_2.png", "post_count": 1, "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "trust_level": 2}], "created_by": {"id": 27408, "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "name": "Jason C", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "last_poster": {"id": 27408, "username": "cosmic-atomic-fan", "name": "Jason C", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "links": [{"url": "https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/rustup", "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "internal": false, "attachment": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 3, "user_id": 33265, "domain": "src.fedoraproject.org", "root_domain": "fedoraproject.org"}, {"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/rustup-package-does-not-provide-rustup/161507/4", "title": "Rustup package does not provide rustup", "internal": true, "attachment": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 2, "user_id": 27408, "domain": "discussion.fedoraproject.org", "root_domain": "fedoraproject.org"}, {"url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rustup/issues/5149", "title": "Better setup experience for third-party packagers? · Issue #5149 · rust-lang/rustup · GitHub", "internal": false, "attachment": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 1, "user_id": 27408, "domain": "github.com", "root_domain": "github.com"}, {"url": "https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/environment-variables.html", "title": "Environment variables - The rustup book", "internal": false, "attachment": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 1, "user_id": 27408, "domain": "rust-lang.github.io", "root_domain": "rust-lang.github.io"}]}, "bookmarks": []}